const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"同一情绪为何影响不同股票？",en:"Why might sentiment affect stocks differently?"},body:{zh:"论文把投机需求变化与套利限制放在一起考虑。估值更主观的公司可能更受乐观或悲观预期影响，难以对冲、卖空成本高的股票也更难被套利力量纠正。这两组特征常有重叠，所以研究并不能轻易把每个结果归给单一渠道。",en:"The argument combines changing speculative demand with limits to arbitrage. Subjective valuations may respond more to optimism or pessimism, while difficult hedging and costly short selling can impede correction. These characteristics overlap, making it difficult to assign each empirical pattern to only one channel."},reference:{url:"https://pages.stern.nyu.edu/~jwurgler/papers/wurgler_baker_cross_section.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2006年期刊版，第1648–1650页",en:"Source: 2006 journal article, pp. 1648–1650"}}},{title:{zh:"六个代理量，不是一份问卷",en:"Six proxies, not a sentiment questionnaire"},body:{zh:"指数使用封闭式基金折价、纽约证交所换手率、IPO数量与首日收益、股票融资占比和股息溢价。它们分别来自市场价格、交易和融资活动。股息溢价比较派息与不派息公司的估值，不能替换为股息率；新闻情感分数也不是这篇论文的原始指标。",en:"The six inputs are closed-end fund discounts, NYSE turnover, IPO volume and first-day returns, the equity share in new issues, and the dividend premium. They describe prices, trading and financing. The dividend premium compares payer and nonpayer valuations; it is not a dividend yield or a text-based news sentiment score."},reference:{url:"https://pages.stern.nyu.edu/~jwurgler/papers/wurgler_baker_cross_section.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2006年期刊版，第1655–1656页",en:"Source: 2006 journal article, pp. 1655–1656"}}},{title:{zh:"共同成分也要考虑先后顺序",en:"Shared variation has a timing structure"},body:{zh:"作者先对六个代理量及其滞后值提取第一主成分，再按与初步指数的相关性为各代理量选择时点，重新构造精简指数。最终组合同时含当期和滞后项，不能把所有观测统一移到同一年而声称保持了原方法。各输入还要先标准化。",en:"A first principal component is estimated from six proxies and their lags. Correlations with that preliminary index then select a timing for each proxy before a parsimonious index is constructed. The final mix uses current and lagged inputs, standardized first; moving every observation to the same year changes the method."},reference:{url:"https://pages.stern.nyu.edu/~jwurgler/papers/wurgler_baker_cross_section.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2006年期刊版，第1656–1657页",en:"Source: 2006 journal article, pp. 1656–1657"}}},{title:{zh:"去除周期成分仍然是模型选择",en:"Removing business-cycle variation is conditional"},body:{zh:"IPO与换手等变量也会随合理的经济变化波动，第一主成分不能自动把共同波动识别为情绪。作者另将各代理量对工业生产、消费增长和衰退指标回归，用残差构造第二指数。这个处理依赖选定的控制变量，不等于剔除了所有基本面信息。",en:"IPO activity and turnover can move for rational economic reasons; a principal component does not label shared variation as sentiment. A second index uses residuals after controlling for industrial production, consumption growth and recessions. Its interpretation remains conditional on those controls, not proof that all fundamental information has disappeared."},reference:{url:"https://pages.stern.nyu.edu/~jwurgler/papers/wurgler_baker_cross_section.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2006年期刊版，第1657页",en:"Source: 2006 journal article, pp. 1657"}}},{title:{zh:"公司特征需要历史匹配",en:"Firm characteristics require historical matching"},body:{zh:"公司资料来自CRSP与Compustat的历史普通股样本，财政年度结束于t−1年的报表与t年7月至次年6月收益匹配。公司年龄按首次进入CRSP计算，并不等同于成立年限。数据覆盖改变会影响解释，跨市场迁移时不能省略这一身份与时间核对。",en:"The historical common-stock sample joins CRSP and Compustat, matching fiscal years ending in t−1 to returns from July t through June t+1. Age measures time since first appearance in CRSP, not time since incorporation. Coverage changes therefore matter when translating the firm's identity and timing conventions to another market."},reference:{url:"https://pages.stern.nyu.edu/~jwurgler/papers/wurgler_baker_cross_section.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2006年期刊版，第1653–1655页",en:"Source: 2006 journal article, pp. 1653–1655"}}},{title:{zh:"不要给复杂特征贴单一标签",en:"Characteristics can carry several meanings"},body:{zh:"高账面市值比既可能反映困境，也包含估值与预期收益信息；销售增长和融资又可能同时对应成长机会或经营压力。论文因此关注情绪与多种特征的关系，而不是把某一比率直接解释为非理性。指数与收益的关系仍需要结合样本和替代解释阅读。",en:"High book-to-market can reflect distress as well as valuation and expected returns; sales growth and financing can describe growth opportunities or operating pressure. The study examines sentiment across such multidimensional characteristics rather than equating one ratio with irrationality. Sample context and competing explanations remain important."},reference:{url:"https://pages.stern.nyu.edu/~jwurgler/papers/wurgler_baker_cross_section.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2006年期刊版，第1655, 1657页",en:"Source: 2006 journal article, pp. 1655, 1657"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"综合情绪指数不是直接观察到的心理状态。共同周期、代理变量的时滞与套利限制都影响解释，历史美国样本的指数权重不是跨市场通用标准。",en:"The composite index is not a direct observation of psychology. Shared cycles, proxy timing and arbitrage constraints affect interpretation; historical US index weights are not a universal cross-market standard."}};export{e as default};
